\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.1}{\ignorespaces Schematic diagram of a statistical inverse problem. The forward operator $K$ maps the latent law $F_0$ to the observable law $G_0$. Statistical inference inverts this map from data $Z_1,\ldots  ,Z_n$. The thesis treats Wicksell's problem ($K$ = stereological transform, Chapters~2--3), nonparametric deconvolution ($K$ = convolution, Chapters~4), and proximal causal inference ($K$ = unobserved confounding mechanism, Chapter~5).}}{1}{figure.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig: inverse problem schematic}{{1.1}{1}{Schematic diagram of a statistical inverse problem. The forward operator $K$ maps the latent law $F_0$ to the observable law $G_0$. Statistical inference inverts this map from data $Z_1,\ldots ,Z_n$. The thesis treats Wicksell's problem ($K$ = stereological transform, Chapters~2--3), nonparametric deconvolution ($K$ = convolution, Chapters~4), and proximal causal inference ($K$ = unobserved confounding mechanism, Chapter~5)}{figure.caption.2}{}}
